      "reviewedAt": "2026-10-03T18:54:26Z",
      "note": "Reviewed anchor, defect, loss and complete age history. Etherscan verified src/REVLoans.sol matches source-3 byte-for-byte. Source-4 callTracer records CREATE2 by 0x4e59b44847b379578588920ca78fbf26c0b4956c. eth_getCode is empty at 23346741 and hashes to the declared runtime at 23346742 and 24917718, as does source-1 prestateTracer code. The direct runtime has no upgrade, delegatecall or destruction path. Pricing dependencies are immutable. The validation and normalization defects exist at deployment, and attacker fake-source registration is their first exercise, not an age reset. Scan eth_getLogs at the target from deployment through block 26113676 for Borrow topic 0x90ac858b09db4f44113a984e09c297b5c0529be26c65a23a1b8967d4124ca5e4. The only three earlier successful loans (blocks 24019253, 24019298, 24450867) use the real 18-decimal ETH source without inflated debt. Source-1 instead passes 0xbd18f03788a4233278f240054d79603f042735e2 as token and terminal, returning decimals 36 and currency 61166. The next transaction drains ETH. Checked all 97 Borrow events and Etherscan txlist/txlistinternal through the coverage block. Later actors and same-code decimal-accounting recurrences join this episode. For each loss source, reproduce debug_traceTransaction(callTracer), discard reverted frames and sum ETH CALL values from terminal 0x2db6d704058e552defe415753465df8df0361846 minus CALL values to it. This removes recycled fees, repayments and retained attacker funding. Include the additional 200000000000 wei input in 0x8b46ca00386889eba1fa5e62c8967c7a21a608132f74de2f896eab4fd9554937. Total depletion: 30.888198825567472318 ETH. No nonzero real ERC20 loss was observed. Each daily component marks its exact wei sum at the nearest DefiLlama ETH quote to that day's first loss transaction. Scope ends at block 26113676. Re-scan later Borrow events on subsequent updates."
    }
